     1	# Anchor sidecars
     2	
     3	An anchor sidecar binds one population to one source document. Each anchor
     4	says where in the document a role value of one fact can be found. `gnd check
     5	--anchors PATH --document PATH` and `gnd verify` read it to evaluate
     6	`anchored` constraints.
     7	
     8	An anchor binds a value to a range of text, nothing more. Neither GND nor the
     9	caller claims that the range entails the fact. Several anchors on one role add
    10	evidence for it; none of them proves it.
    11	
    12	The parser, `gnd.anchors.parse_anchor_sidecar`, is the authority for this
    13	format. [`anchor-sidecar.schema.json`](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/src/gnd/anchor-sidecar.schema.json)
    14	describes the part a JSON Schema can express, and a test keeps the two in
    15	step.
    16	
    17	## The file
    18	
    19	The sidecar sits next to its population as `<population>.anchors.json`:
    20	
    21	```json
    22	{
    23	  "schema_version": 2,
    24	  "population_sha256": "<SHA-256 of the population file's raw bytes>",
    25	  "vocabulary_digest": "<digest of the model's vocabulary>",
    26	  "document_sha256": "<SHA-256 of the document's raw bytes>",
    27	  "anchors": [
    28	    {
    29	      "fact_key": {"fact_type": "record_has_label", "roles": {"record": "R-1", "label": "Café Alpha"}},
    30	      "role": "label",
    31	      "span": {"start": 27, "end": 37},
    32	      "occurrence": 0,
    33	      "excerpt_sha256": "<SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of the NFC document slice>"
    34	    }
    35	  ]
    36	}
    37	```
    38	
    39	- `fact_key` names one fact by its fact type and every role value.
    40	- `role` is the role whose value the anchor points at.
    41	- `span` is a half-open range of Unicode code points in the NFC-normalized
    42	  document.
    43	- `occurrence` counts matches of the value from zero across the whole
    44	  document; the selected match must lie wholly inside the span.
    45	- `block_id` and `unit_id` are optional, non-empty labels for your own use.
    46	
    47	`vocabulary_digest` is the canonical JSON digest of the model's object types
    48	and fact types, leaving out object type descriptions and each fact type's
    49	derivation rule, constraints, sample population and dependencies. The
    50	[constraint reference](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/blob/main/src/gnd/skills/gnd-orm-core/references/constraint-reference.md)
    51	gives the matching rules.
    52	
    53	## Versions 1 and 2
    54	
    55	The two versions have the same keys and still bind one population to one
    56	document. They differ in which anchors count as the same:
    57	
    58	| Version | One anchor is identified by | Refused when repeated |
    59	|---|---|---|
    60	| 1 | fact key and role | `duplicate fact-role anchor`: one anchor per fact role |
    61	| 2 | fact key, role, span start and end, occurrence | `duplicate anchor`: several anchors per fact role are allowed |
    62	
    63	In version 2, the same range with a different `excerpt_sha256` is still a
    64	duplicate: one range has one excerpt. No `gnd` command writes a sidecar; the
    65	extractor does, and `gnd.anchors.write_anchor_sidecar` publishes either version.
    66	
    67	## When a role with several anchors passes
    68	
    69	Every anchor on the role must hold: the value's selected occurrence must lie
    70	inside the anchor's span. Each anchor is a claim about the
    71	document, so one wrong anchor fails the role even when another is right. The
    72	failed fact is reported once per role, however many of its anchors fail. The
    73	order of anchors in the file does not change the result.
    74	
    75	## What the parser refuses
    76	
    77	A malformed sidecar exits 3 with `anchor:sidecar-invalid`. Besides the shape
    78	the schema describes, the parser refuses:
    79	
    80	| Rule | Example |
    81	|---|---|
    82	| A repeated anchor identity (per version, above) | the same anchor twice |
    83	| `start` not below `end` | `{"start": 5, "end": 5}` |
    84	| A file over 1 MiB | about 3,500 anchors fit |
    85	| Duplicate JSON keys | `"schema_version"` twice |
    86	| `NaN`, `Infinity` or a number too large for a float | a role value `NaN`, `1e400` |
    87	| Integer literals over 18 characters, sign included | an occurrence of `10**18` |
    88	| Nesting deeper than 32 | |
    89	| Integer-valued floats where integers are required | `"start": 27.0` |
    90	| Invalid UTF-8 | |
    91	
    92	A sidecar whose digests do not match the population, the document or the
    93	model, or whose excerpt does not match its span, is refused before any value
    94	is checked, also exit 3. This digest match is the binding; whether each value
    95	is found inside its span is the `anchored` verdict, which can fail (exit 1).

